Tracing policy:
- Judge the two documents only against each other. Do not judge whether either is correct, complete or well written, and do not use outside knowledge of the software.
- A trace link requires that one item states, refines or realises the specific content of the other. Shared vocabulary or a shared generic concern is not enough: "the system shall be reliable" does not trace to a goal unless that goal concerns the same reliability property.
- Generic requirements that would hold for almost any software (e.g. "shall log errors", "shall be maintainable") trace only to items that state the same concern.
- An item may have several links. An empty link list is a valid and expected answer when nothing in the other document supports the item.
- Use the identifiers exactly as they appear. List every requirement of the requirements document, in document order, exactly once, including requirements without links.
- Keep each item text to at most ten words; it only identifies the item.
